Cra: a page Cra hosts sees its own column as its window. Cra's pages sit in
Cra's window beside its sidebar, not in a window of Chrome's, and Chrome gave
them the whole NSWindow as their window: window.outerWidth - innerWidth was
the sidebar's width (345 in a normal window). Sites read that as DevTools being
open. Discord then takes its sign-in token out of localStorage until its page
goes, so every other Discord tab opened on its login page while one was open.
The page's window (outerWidth, outerHeight, screenX, screenY) is now its
column, from the window's top to the page's bottom, as a page in Chrome's
window sees it, and it follows the page when the sidebar slides. The page's
own bounds (GetViewBounds: popups, IME, drag) are unchanged, and so is every
page in a window of Chrome's (one with a parent ui::Layer).

